  "details": "1. Use the open beta branch for the IK behavior changes (previously part of IK beta, presumably live after August 31st 2023)\n\n2. Load up any instance\n\n3. Cover your controllers or cause them to lose tracking by other means, while remaining connected.\n\n4. Watch the hands snap towards the center point of the playspace, moving around the center point will always have the arms aligned towards the center, as if the controllers were placed on the floor.\n\nThis periodically affects trackers as well under certain conditions (seems to be when losing/regaining tracking in succession) so instead of freezing in place they teleport to the center.\n\nEDIT: A reliable reproduction method on trackers: \n\n1. Enable \"Freeze tracking on disconnect\".\n\n2. Freeze a tracker under a blanket (new IK behavior).\n\n3. Power off the tracker (remains frozen with \"Freeze tracking on disconnect\").\n\n4. Power on the tracker and watch it teleport to the center of the play space (tracker indicators when the big menu is open will appear at the center of the play space).\n\nEDIT 2: Tracker video https://youtu.be/GHNKY4c5zVI",
